        "Gjsc0VGf7v_9_ZS-0NPAj",
        "9kIfEsLQk2sTJthq2nTJb"
      ],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b32O",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 2055855956,
      "version": 355,
      "versionNonce": 1503348315,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [
        {
          "id": "lLScMsdW3pLe3ISt4KNoR",
          "type": "arrow"
        }
      ],
      "updated": 1789416637430,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "In a particularly disturbing example,\nRadford et al. (2021) documented a\n9.2% increase in object lassification\naccuracy when fine-tuning a computer\nvision model on the ImageNet dataset\nwithout observing any improvement in\naverage accuracy when classifying the\nsame objects on seven other natural\nimage datasets. ",
      "fontSize": 16,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "In a particularly disturbing example, Radford et al. (2021) documented a 9.2% increase in object lassification accuracy when fine-tuning a computer vision model on the ImageNet dataset\nwithout observing any improvement in average accuracy when classifying the same objects on seven other natural\nimage datasets. ",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
