      "seed": 1858759404,
      "version": 942,
      "versionNonce": 360154651,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1789416637430,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Multitask Training",
      "fontSize": 28,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Multitask Training",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "9tKuALKPj1F6WlsWKsgSc",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -3846.865724346732,
      "y": 4166.695614556073,
      "width": 934.6541748046875,
      "height": 725,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [
        "wehyOG0nJn74sQ2Ua0I6a",
        "MSXjd5ovKQUudYZqfRRBf",
        "repOYft3kSDE5X62e2Iah",
        "9kIfEsLQk2sTJthq2nTJb"
      ],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b32l",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1954895828,
      "version": 1737,
      "versionNonce": 1853229755,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1789416637430,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "A fully featured speech recognition system can involve many additional components \n    1. voice activity detection\n    2. speaker diarization\n    3. text normalization\n\nThey used special tokens to specify all tasks and conditioning information the decoder. \n\nThey also train the decoder to condition on the history of text of the transcript in to make\nit learn to use longer-range text context to resolve ambiguous audio. Specifically, with some\nprobability they added the transcript text preceding the current audio segment to the\ndecoder’s context. \n\nStart Token: indicate the beginning of prediction with a <|startoftranscript|> token.\n\nLanguage Token: the model first predict the language being spoken which is represented by a\nunique token for each language in our training set (99 total). \n\nNo Speech Token: in the case where there is no speech in an audio segment, the model is\ntrained to predict a <|nospeech|> token indicating this. \n\nTask Token: the next token specifies the task (either transcription or translation) with an\n<|transcribe|> or <|translate|> token. \n\nTimestamp Token: after this, add a token to specify whether to predict timestamps or not by\nincluding a <|notimestamps|> token for that case. For timestamp prediction, we interleave their\nprediction with the caption tokens: the start time token is predicted before each caption’s\ntext, and the end time token is predicted after.\n\nEnd Token: Lastly add a <|endoftranscript|> token.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "A fully featured speech recognition system can involve many additional components \n    1. voice activity detection\n    2. speaker diarization\n    3. text normalization\n\nThey used special tokens to specify all tasks and conditioning information the decoder. \n\nThey also train the decoder to condition on the history of text of the transcript in to make it learn to use longer-range text context to resolve ambiguous audio. Specifically, with some probability they added the transcript text preceding the current audio segment to the decoder’s context. \n\nStart Token: indicate the beginning of prediction with a <|startoftranscript|> token.\n\nLanguage Token: the model first predict the language being spoken which is represented by a unique token for each language in our training set (99 total). \n\nNo Speech Token: in the case where there is no speech in an audio segment, the model is trained to predict a <|nospeech|> token indicating this. \n\nTask Token: the next token specifies the task (either transcription or translation) with an <|transcribe|> or <|translate|> token. \n\nTimestamp Token: after this, add a token to specify whether to predict timestamps or not by including a <|notimestamps|> token for that case. For timestamp prediction, we interleave their prediction with the caption tokens: the start time token is predicted before each caption’s text, and the end time token is predicted after.\n\nEnd Token: Lastly add a <|endoftranscript|> token.",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
