    {
      "id": "JWsOkUdbyCjUUfa0CTbX7",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -997.2401210077056,
      "y": 2372.2776607526594,
      "width": 934.6541748046875,
      "height": 1075,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [
        "J-0-qqocLQCtwXfb5xX0W",
        "-Le2EcnadaZi6Szrqc6m0",
        "EA_tr5suNeOhWDvJz2_DF"
      ],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b36l",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1179590356,
      "version": 1079,
      "versionNonce": 795847477,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1789416511819,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Pseudo-labeling transfers only the final sequence selected by the teacher. But the teacher\ncontains more information than its final transcription.\n\nAt every decoding step, Whisper produces a probability distribution over the entire vocabulary.\nKL divergence allows the student to learn from the whole teacher distribution.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nThe addition of the KL-divergence term yields an OOD word error rate (WER) that is 0.3%\nabsolute lower compared to just PL. This suggests that the additional information transferred\nfrom the teacher to the student during KD is beneficial over training on PL alone.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nThe typical setting in layer-based compression is that the dimensionality of the student model\nmatches that of the teacher model. This means the student and teacher layers output the\nsame shape of hidden-states. Thus, we can introduce a mean-square error (MSE) term to\nencourage the student’s hidden layer outputs to match those of the teacher:\n\n\n\n\n\nIncorporating the MSE loss term had a negligible effect on the average WER performance of\nthe distilled model. This indicates that there is sufficient training signal from the PL and KL\nloss terms. The MSE loss requires that the hidden-states for each layer are recorded and\nkept in memory. This added a significant overhead when training the model in JAX, which\nresulted in a decrease to the maximum possible batch size. Therefore, our final KD training\nobjective is a weighted sum of the PL and KL terms only.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Pseudo-labeling transfers only the final sequence selected by the teacher. But the teacher contains more information than its final transcription.\n\nAt every decoding step, Whisper produces a probability distribution over the entire vocabulary. KL divergence allows the student to learn from the whole teacher distribution.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nThe addition of the KL-divergence term yields an OOD word error rate (WER) that is 0.3% absolute lower compared to just PL. This suggests that the additional information transferred from the teacher to the student during KD is beneficial over training on PL alone.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nThe typical setting in layer-based compression is that the dimensionality of the student model\nmatches that of the teacher model. This means the student and teacher layers output the same shape of hidden-states. Thus, we can introduce a mean-square error (MSE) term to encourage the student’s hidden layer outputs to match those of the teacher:\n\n\n\n\n\nIncorporating the MSE loss term had a negligible effect on the average WER performance of the distilled model. This indicates that there is sufficient training signal from the PL and KL loss terms. The MSE loss requires that the hidden-states for each layer are recorded and kept in memory. This added a significant overhead when training the model in JAX, which resulted in a decrease to the maximum possible batch size. Therefore, our final KD training objective is a weighted sum of the PL and KL terms only.",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "tUUFQMEbGF74CrKYBckJf",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -618.3720586704662,
      "y": 2306.444327419326,
      "width": 186.84475708007812,
      "height": 35,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
