    {
      "id": "CdETTNf3WLx_tNBfbUe84",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -1015.1932062502294,
      "y": -4.433099641475906,
      "width": 934.6541748046875,
      "height": 1125,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [
        "IGjcHFqy2_NvPkgVq5qAi",
        "EA_tr5suNeOhWDvJz2_DF"
      ],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b38l",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 32978516,
      "version": 1118,
      "versionNonce": 1836983221,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1789416511819,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "As the size of pre-trained speech recognition models increases, running these large models in\nlow-latency or resource-constrained environments becomes challenging. \n\nThe original whisoer has 1.5B parameters\n\nIn this work, the authors distilled the Whisper model into a smaller variant, called Distil-\nWhisper. \n\nThe distilled model is 5.8 times faster with 51% fewer parameters, while performing to within\n1% WER on out-of-distribution test data in a zero-shot transfer setting.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nThey distill 2-layer decoder checkpoints from the medium.en and large-v2 models by copying the\nfirst and last decoder layers, which we refer to as distil-medium.en and distil-large-v2\nrespectively.\n\n\n\n\n\nThey assembled a large corpus of ASR training data for large-scale KD through a combination\nof nine publicly available speech recognition datasets. The combined dataset contains 21,170\nhours of speech data, encompassing over 18,260 speakers and 10 distinct domains.\n\nThey generate pseudo-labels for our training data with the Whisper large-v2 checkpoint and\nused them with cross entropy loss.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "As the size of pre-trained speech recognition models increases, running these large models in low-latency or resource-constrained environments becomes challenging. \n\nThe original whisoer has 1.5B parameters\n\nIn this work, the authors distilled the Whisper model into a smaller variant, called Distil-Whisper. \n\nThe distilled model is 5.8 times faster with 51% fewer parameters, while performing to within 1% WER on out-of-distribution test data in a zero-shot transfer setting.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nThey distill 2-layer decoder checkpoints from the medium.en and large-v2 models by copying the first and last decoder layers, which we refer to as distil-medium.en and distil-large-v2 respectively.\n\n\n\n\n\nThey assembled a large corpus of ASR training data for large-scale KD through a combination of nine publicly available speech recognition datasets. The combined dataset contains 21,170 hours of speech data, encompassing over 18,260 speakers and 10 distinct domains.\n\nThey generate pseudo-labels for our training data with the Whisper large-v2 checkpoint and used them with cross entropy loss.",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
